# config/tmp-alert-threshold - the /tmp usage percent at or above which
# firstmate warns, at every session-start bootstrap (bin/fm-bootstrap.sh's
# tmp_alert_check) and on the watcher's periodic sweep between sessions
# (bin/fm-watch.sh's tmp_alert_scan). Copy this into a local, gitignored
# config/tmp-alert-threshold and replace the value below with your own.
#
# A single integer 0-100, read from the first non-empty, non-comment line;
# blank lines and full-line "#" comments are ignored. Usage is read via
# `df -P /tmp`. An ABSENT or empty config/tmp-alert-threshold is a no-op, and
# a threshold line that fails to parse as an integer 0-100 is treated the
# same way. A host without `df` on PATH but a configured threshold prints a
# one-time TMP_USAGE_INERT diagnostic instead of silently never alerting.
#
# The value below is an illustrative placeholder - pick a threshold that
# leaves enough headroom for this machine's own /tmp usage pattern.
80
